{
  "format": "call-of-slop-construct-part/1",
  "name": "Panel Former",
  "description": "A Panel Former Core: a stretch former that forms body panels by order, each from one blank, on the bed of Bed Blocks welded beside it (2 x 2 m each, up to 32 x 32 m), its Core beside the bed's head and an Out Table on the bed's far end. A Roller Tile run butted on the bed's head rolls each blank in; the jaws grip it and a die of columns rises from the pocket under the bed and stretches it to shape. The largest panel is the bed's rectangle. A blank is a flat extruded sheet of the panel's material and thickness, its flat size to 25% over; the trim drops into its offcut bin. Needs power.",
